==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|novo}}, from {{inh|pt|la|novus||new}}, from {{inh|pt|itc-pro|*nowos}}, from {{inh|pt|ine-pro|*néwos||new}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT|Brazil}} {{IPA|/ˈno.vu/|lang=pt}}
* {{audio|Pt novo.ogg|Audio|lang=pt}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/ˈno.vo/|lang=pt}}

===Adjective===
{{pt-adj|nov|o}}

# {{l|en|new}} {{gloss|recently made or created}}
#: {{ux|pt|É uma casa '''nova'''.|t=It is a '''new''' house.}}
# {{l|en|new}} {{gloss|not previously worn or used}}
#: {{ux|pt|Comprei um carro '''novo'''.|t=I bough a '''new''' car.}}
# {{l|en|new}} {{gloss|recently discovered}}
#: {{ux|pt|As '''novas''' ruínas serão úteis aos arqueólogos.|t=The '''new''' ruins will be useful to archaeologists.}}
# {{l|en|new}}; {{l|en|young}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ele é '''novo''' demais para assistir isso.|t=He is too '''young''' to watch this.}}
# {{l|en|original}} {{gloss|fresh; different}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ideias '''novas''' para tempos novos.|t='''Original''' ideas for new times.}}
# {{lb|pt|of a period of time|often follows the noun}} {{l|en|new}} {{gloss|about to begin or recently begun}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ano '''novo'''.|t='''New''' year.}}

====Inflection====
{{pt-adj-infl|nov|o}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|not previously word or used}} {{l|pt|novo em folha}}
* {{sense|young}} {{l|pt|jovem}}, {{l|pt|novato}}
